      DependencyIndex: 9
      LevelID: 10
      NodeType: 3
      Ports:
        Description:
          String: ""
        DescriptionText:
          ClassType1: TEXT
          String: |-
            Matcap reflections are a cheap way of doing reflection. The reflection is created by sampling from a spherical texture instead of actual scene data. This technique is also sometimes referred to as material capture ("MatCap") reflection. The reference texture only stores one side of a sphere.
            
            Inputs:
            Matcap Reflection Texture - The sphereical reflection map used to sample lighting.
            Intensity - The strength of the reflection effect.
            Normal Space: The space that the normal input is provided in. You can use World Space or Tangent Space (Normal Map) normals as input.
            Normal: The surface normal.
        FirstTime:
          Variable: false
        Locked:
          Variable: false
        SubGraphUniqueID130:
          Variable: [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]
        SubGraphUniqueID131:
          ClassType2: TEXTURE_OBJECT_2D
          Connection0:
            NodeLevelID: 12
            PortID: Texture
        SubGraphUniqueID132:
          Variable: [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]
        SubGraphUniqueID133:
          ItemIndex: 1
          ItemList: "World : Tangent (Normal Map)"
        SubGraphUniqueID137:
          IOType: 1
          Variable: [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]
        Title1:
          String: Matcap Reflection
